  "preamble": "Deletion of the labiodental fricative [f], removing the segment entirely. It is regular in Micronesian, where Proto-Micronesian *f was lost in Kiribati and Marshallese, and occurs after /l/ in Scots (Old English self > sel, twelf > twal).",
  "phoneticEffects": "Deletion, Apocope",
  "languageExamples": [
    {
      "language": "Scots",
      "languageFamily": "Anglic",
      "examples": [
        {
          "from": "Middle English self (Old English self)",
          "to": "sel 'self'",
          "note": "Final /f/ was lost after /l/."
        },
        {
          "from": "Early Scots twelf (Old English twelf)",
          "to": "twal 'twelve'",
          "note": "Same loss of /f/ after /l/; the alternative forms twel and twol also lack it."
        }
      ]
